Phase 5b of the taint-correctness campaign, plus WI-nibav's verified drop-in.

1. CROSS-LANGUAGE POLLUTION, and the function written to prevent it had ZERO
   production callers. cmd_verify_claims selects a language's edges with
   src.startswith(lang:) OR dst.startswith(lang:). The OR is CORRECT and stays --
   the propagation BFS needs both endpoints to walk a cross-language call -- but
   it hands a bridge edge python:... -> go:... to BOTH languages' matchers, so a
   `go:` callee can be looked up in the Python index. The guard therefore belongs
   at the MATCH, not the selection: _match_propagation_entry now takes the
   language whose catalogue built the index and refuses a foreign callee before
   any lookup. _extract_callee_language's docstring has always claimed it is
   "used by sink/source matching to filter cross-language pollution"; its only
   reachability was its own unit test (a WI-ratuv family member). A test now
   asserts the matcher references it so prose and code cannot drift again.

   MEASURED, AND IT MOVES NOTHING TODAY: the 9-repo cohort holds 208
   cross-language taint call edges (95% typescript<->javascript) and ZERO match a
   sink in the wrong language's index. A latent guard, reported as one. The dead
   docstring's "thousands of false positives" from an elixir/Python `get`
   collision is NOT validated here -- the cohort has no elixir -- and is left as
   an untested assertion rather than repeated as a result. The parameter defaults
   to "" so every existing caller and test is unaffected.

2. TaintFlowFinding.to_dict DROPPED THE THREE FIELDS THAT CANNOT BE RECOVERED
   FROM THE EMITTED SYMBOL. source_module / sink_module (the module a catalog
   entry declared, WI-joruv) and source_boundary (the io_primitives boundary the
   source came from, WI-vazal) were absent, so a serialized finding was strictly
   weaker than the object it came from. verify-claims survived only because it
   reaches the dataclass directly; any consumer of the serialized form silently
   lost the WI-vazal split that shipped specifically to be readable. The guard
   asserts the PROPERTY -- every declared field appears in to_dict -- rather than
   the three names, so a fourth cannot be dropped silently.

3. ujson CATALOGUED, orjson DELIBERATELY NOT (WI-nibav). Both were candidates
   from the cohort enumeration and the item's own rule is "read the package, do
   not assume the surface". Read: ujson exposes dump/dumps/load/loads and so
   mirrors the catalogued json.dump file-write; orjson exposes only dumps/loads,
   has NO dump, and therefore has no file-write surface -- cataloguing it would
   match nothing. Pinned by a test so a later completeness pass does not add it
   by symmetry.

   defusedcsv is NOT added, because the blocker is elsewhere. Its real API is the
   defusedcsv.csv SUBMODULE, and the analyzer emits module=defusedcsv,
   name=csv.writer for `from defusedcsv import csv; csv.writer(...)`. Verified
   against the live pretix edge: the conventional declaration (module:
   defusedcsv.csv, functions: [writer]) does NOT match, and only a dotted NAME
   does -- a form used by exactly 1 of 1979 built-in primitives. The catalogue
   should not contort to fit a malformed id; filed as an analyzer module/name
   split defect instead.

Verified: 10 tests, 9 red before the change; core package 10,939 passed; mypy
ratchet 672 = 672 delta +0; smart-test 4,352 passed over 101 selected files;
ruff clean; language gate asserted non-destructive on the cohort.

